-- title:
--   Top differential forms over F form the line spanned by ρ
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative domain with $K$ a field that is a fraction field of $R$, let $O$ be a commutative domain which is an $R$-algebra, and let $F$ be a field that is a fraction field of $O$; assume $F$ is also a $K$-algebra and an $R$-algebra, with the scalar towers $R \to O \to F$ and $R \to K \to F$ compatible. Let $d$ be a natural number and let $b$ be a basis of the module of Kähler differentials $\Omega_{O/R}$ over $O$ indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,d$. Regard the $F$-module $\bigwedge^d_F \Omega_{F/K}$ as an $O$-module by restriction of scalars along $O \to F$, and let $\rho$ be the value at the canonical wedge $b_0 \wedge \dots \wedge b_{d-1}$ of the $O$-linear map $\bigwedge^d_O \Omega_{O/R} \to \bigwedge^d_F \Omega_{F/K}$ corresponding, under the universal property of the exterior power, to the alternating map `ιMultiAlong R K O F d`. The assertion is twofold: $\rho \neq 0$, and for every $\omega \in \bigwedge^d_F \Omega_{F/K}$ there is $a \in F$ with $\omega = a \cdot \rho$; that is, $\bigwedge^d_F \Omega_{F/K} = F\rho$ is a line generated by $\rho$.
--
--   This is the freeness-of-rank-one statement for top differential forms at the generic fibre: if $\Omega_{O/R}$ is free of rank $d$, the top exterior power of $\Omega_{F/K}$ is the $F$-line spanned by the image of a basis wedge. It supplies the non-vanishing side condition and the comparison coefficient $a$ used in the results on orders of top forms and on reading off components, such as [`NeronModelInfra.TopFormOrder.eq_addOrd_and_bijective_mapBaseChange_of_topFormMap_eq_of_addOrd_le`](thm.html#NeronModelInfra.TopFormOrder.eq_addOrd_and_bijective_mapBaseChange_of_topFormMap_eq_of_addOrd_le) and [`NeronModelInfra.ComponentReading.eq_n_of_forall_topFormMap_eq_mul_zpow_smul`](thm.html#NeronModelInfra.ComponentReading.eq_n_of_forall_topFormMap_eq_mul_zpow_smul).
